# Home Dark custom-card source-first workflow

For every custom Lovelace card change, update or create the local JavaScript source
under `home-dark-cards/` first. Treat that local source/scratchpad file as the
behavioral source of truth; use the `home-assistant` MCP server to publish/sync
the JavaScript resource in Home Assistant, not to replace the local source.

Only after the resource is successfully registered or updated may you change the
dashboard configuration to consume the new behavior. Use the existing resource
ID with an optimistic hash/cache-busting URL when appropriate; do not create
duplicate resources for an existing card. Verify both the published resource
(ID, URL/content or preview, and type) and the final dashboard configuration.
Never edit Home Assistant `.storage` files or local HA configuration directly.

## Resource hosting

- Never create or update inline Lovelace resources for custom cards.
- Keep every custom-card implementation in a local file under
  `home-dark-cards/`.
- For a URL-mode custom-card change, assume the user has copied the updated
  local file to `/config/www/home-dark-cards/` once the local edit is complete.
  Immediately update the existing resource with a new cache-busting URL; do not
  wait for copy confirmation unless the user explicitly says they have not
  copied it.
- Register or update only URL-mode module resources at
  `/local/home-dark-cards/<file>.js`, reusing the existing resource ID when
  available. Do not create duplicate resources.
- Inspect the live resource registry before dashboard work. If the dashboard
  uses an inline resource, explicitly tell the user and do not silently update
  or replace it.
